  "description": "NEZRUJ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H88 Cl6 La4 Mn2 O25,2(C3 H8 O2),0.5(I2). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La4 (La) has 8 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.373-5.756 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.87-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C36H88Cl6La4Mn2O25. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
